{
  "series": "K",
  "title": "K_eff modulation: nested lighting policies with 48 / 240 / 480 / 960 reachable actions",
  "created": "2026-09-04",
  "design_rules": [
    "K_eff = (colors + 1) * (emotions + 1) * intensities; the +1 is the 'none' state, the fallback tuple is the (none, none) cell.",
    "Policies are nested: every item of K48 is in K240 (the production policy), every item of K240 is in K480, every item of K480 is in K960.",
    "Composition order is unchanged from resolve_case_output(): colour target -> + emotion adjust -> + intensity adjust -> normalise (hue mod 360, S/B/Dimmer clamp 0..100, CT clamp 153..500) -> snap hue to anchor if circular distance > 18.",
    "|emotion dH| <= 4 and |intensity dH| <= 3 everywhere, so the 18-degree snap can never fire (max drift 7 degrees), exactly as in the production policy.",
    "Colour CT follows the warm/cool convention of the production anchors (red 255 ... blue 410): warm hues low mired, cool hues high mired.",
    "New emotion phrase lists avoid words already used by production emotions (e.g. 설레/신나 belong to happiness, 무서워 to anxiety, 외로워 to sadness)."
  ],
  "safe_fallback": {
    "H": 45,
    "S": 20,
    "B": 56,
    "Dimmer": 56,
    "CT": 300
  },
